      "content": "<p></p><h2><b>Historical Background of Hennur</b></h2>Hennur has a rich history, that dates back to decades. This was a small village at the outskirts of Bangalore. When the city started to spread and urbanize, it gained momentum as a locality in <a href=\"https://www.kots.world/blog/the-ultimate-guide-to-hennur-all-you-need-to-know#:~:text=In%20conclusion%2C%20Hennur%20is%20a,the%20city's%20real%20estate%20landscape.\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 255);\">Hennur</span>.</a> It actually caught momentum with the Outer Ring Road development, which gave them easy connectivity to the city of Bangalore.<p></p><h4><b><br>Evolution Over Time</b></h4><p><b>Early Days:</b>Hennur was an agricultural region with very few residential layouts<br><b>Urban Development: </b>IT parks and commercial spaces have been erected and brought professionals and families.<br><b>Current Status:</b> Hennur has today modern residential complexes, shopping centers, and recreational facilities.</p><h2><b><br>Location and Connectivity</b></h2><p>One of the standout features of Hennur is its strategic location. Situated along the Outer Ring Road, it provides easy access to major areas in Bangalore.</p><h4><b><br>Key Connectivity Points</b></h4><p><b>Proximity to IT Parks:</b> Hennur is close to Manyata Tech Park, making it ideal for IT professionals.<br><b>Transport Links:</b>The biggest positive of Hennur Road is its proximity to the International Airport, which can be reached within 45 minutes from here. What’s more, it is easily reachable without having to bother much about the city traffic, which saves a resident of this area plenty of time and provides them relief! Hennur Road is also well-connected to other parts of the city with regular BMTC buses connecting it to major hubs such as Hebbal and Majestic.</p><p></p><p><br>The nearest rail station to Hennur, in terms of rail connectivity, is K.R. Puram and Banaswadi, which both lie within 12 - 14 km. Among them, K.R. Puram is an important halt for long distance inter-city trains. For those preferring to travel by the Namma Metro, the nearest station, Byappanahalli is also within 10 km from here.<br></p><h4><b><span style=\"vertical-align: baseline;\"><br>Distance from Key Locations</span><span style=\"vertical-align: baseline;\">:</span></b></h4><p></p><div><table data-theme=\"{\" themename\":\"theme1\",\"themeobj\":{\"tblpr\":{\"cell\":{\"borders\":{\"border-top\":{\"color\":\"\",\"width\":\"1px\",\"type\":\"solid\"},\"border-right\":{\"color\":\"\",\"width\":\"1px\",\"type\":\"solid\"},\"border-left\":{\"color\":\"\",\"width\":\"1px\",\"type\":\"solid\"},\"border-bottom\":{\"color\":\"\",\"width\":\"1px\",\"type\":\"solid\"}}}}}}\"=\"\" data-cols=\"[{\" wt\":\"5.156in\"},{\"wt\":\"1.469in\"}]\"=\"\" data-width=\"6.63in\" data-table-name=\"Table_1\" data-theader=\"3\" class=\"zw-table\" style=\"margin-left: 0in;\"><tbody><tr data-row-info=\"{\" id\":\"rw-6o3emlj5hur9\",\"type\":\"row\"}\"=\"\"><td class=\"zw-td\" col-index=\"0\" data-cell-height=\"auto\" style=\"border-width: 1.06667px 0px 0px 1.06667px; border-color: rgb(0, 0, 0) rgb(229, 231, 235) rgb(229, 231, 235) rgb(0, 0, 0); padding: 0px; vertical-align: top; width: 494.976px; height: auto;\"><p data-header=\"0\" class=\"zw-paragraph heading0\" data-textformat=\"{\" fgc\":\"rgb(0,=\"\" 0,=\"\" 0)\",\"size\":\"10.50\",\"type\":\"text\"}\"=\"\" data-margin-bottom=\"12pt\" data-hd-info=\"0\" data_styles=\"{\" data-line-height=\"1.2\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 12pt; margin-left: 0px; line-height: 1.2;\"><span style=\"font-family: Roboto; font-size: 10.5pt; vertical-align: baseline;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<b> &nbsp;&nbsp;</b></span><span style=\"vertical-align: baseline;\"><b>Location</b></span></p></td><td class=\"zw-td\" col-index=\"1\" data-cell-height=\